# Agent roles

Orga Drone uses four specialized project subagents under `.cursor/agents/`.
The main agent remains the implementer.

| Role | Subagent | Use when |
|------|----------|----------|
| Product-Spec-Reviewer | `product-spec-reviewer` | Review an existing product spec vs code/docs; no code changes |
| Product-UX-Designer | `product-ux-designer` | Meaningful UI/interaction work after PM; usability discovery; no code; no implementation issues |
| Engineering-Planner | `engineering-planner` | Approved spec (and PM-selected UX concept when UI) → technical plan; research first (Plan Mode) |
| Implementation-Reviewer | `implementation-reviewer` | Review diff/tests/docs/risks before commit |

Workflow:

1. Spec written (human / product)
2. Product-Spec-Reviewer → approve / revise
3. Product-UX-Designer → discovery/audit when UI/interaction is meaningful (skip otherwise)
4. PM selects the product direction (same issue)
5. Engineering-Planner → plan
6. Main agent → implement
7. Implementation-Reviewer → pre-commit review
8. Commit only when the user explicitly asks

Delegate to these subagents when the user names the role or the task clearly matches. Do not skip Product-Spec-Reviewer for large product claims unless the user waives it. Do not skip Product-UX-Designer for meaningful UI/interaction work unless the user waives it or the change is a simple bug fix, backend-only, CI/tooling, or a migration without user-facing impact.
